# TypeScript & React Development Rules

## React Best Practices
- Use **functional components** with hooks (no class components)
- Prefer `React.FC` type annotation for components when needed
- Use proper TypeScript interfaces for props and state
- Import React types from `@types/react` when needed

## TypeScript Standards
- Use **interfaces** over types for object shapes
- Provide explicit return types for functions
- Use proper generics for reusable components
- Follow the TypeScript configs in [packages/typescript-config/](mdc:packages/typescript-config/)

## Import Patterns
```tsx
import React from 'react';
import { ComponentProps } from 'react';
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button';
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils';
```

## Component Structure
```tsx
interface MyComponentProps {
  title: string;
  optional?: boolean;
}

export function MyComponent({ title, optional = false }: MyComponentProps) {
  return <div>{title}</div>;
}
```

## Hooks Usage
- Use `useState`, `useEffect`, `useCallback`, `useMemo` appropriately
- Custom hooks should start with `use` prefix
- Keep hooks at the top of component function

## Event Handlers
```tsx
const handleClick = useCallback((event: React.MouseEvent<HTMLButtonElement>) => {
  // handler logic
}, [dependencies]);
```